Last week (11.10-11.14) the total number of Su Ke Pan transactions was 5 trading days, overall showing a trend of 'first rising and then falling, profit withdrawal':
#BTC #ETH 
1. Earnings Summary

   BTC: 25 transactions, total space 25,518 points, equivalent to approximately ¥151,722 (based on 1 point ≈ ¥5.95).

   ETH: 17 transactions, total space 1,294 points, equivalent to approximately ¥129,400 (based on 1 point ≈ ¥100).

   Total dual currency: approximately 281,122, average daily 56.2k.

2. Rhythm Review

   ① Monday (11.10) bullish momentum, ETH single-day 39883 space created the highest of the week;

   ② Tuesday and Wednesday high-level fluctuations, short-term reversal shorts began to harvest, profits still maintained at 40-50k/day;

   ③ Thursday and Friday trend turned down, the proportion of shorts increased, but the bullish early morning chasing caused some pullback, Thursday's space suddenly dropped to 28663, and Friday further shrank to 21403, the lowest of the week.

3. Issues and Improvements
   - On the trend reversal day (11.12 night) the long position stop loss was slow, BTC single transaction floating loss -6342, lowering the net profit of the day;
   - Friday morning ETH chasing long 3232→3146, single day 86 points stop loss exposed concentrated risk;
   - Although the short reversal direction was correct, the exit was too early, missing the subsequent market of 2000+ points.

4. Next Week's Plan
   - Continue to execute the discipline of 'not chasing orders in the early session, reducing positions first during trend reversals', tighten the stop loss point to 1.5 times ATR;
   - After shorts profit ≥100 points, set price protection to prevent roller coaster rides;
   - Friday night trading has shown the embryonic form of bottom divergence, gradually take profit on shorts, waiting for bullish signals after stabilizing in the 96k/3000 range.

Overall, last week's profit was 281,000, a decline of about 20% compared to the previous week (estimated 350,000), mainly due to the trend reversal day pullback. Maintaining profits, reducing frequency, and improving the profit-loss ratio are the core goals for this week.
